click=\"edStarFav(this)\">★</span><span class=\"ed-star\" data-star=\"2\" onclick=\"edStarFav(this)\">★</span><span class=\"ed-star\" data-star=\"3\" onclick=\"edStarFav(this)\">★</span>\n          </span>\n        </span>\n        \n        \n        \n        <div class=\"back_order_area\">\n          <p class=\"cart-btn\">\n            \n            <a class=\"respo order_set_target js-loading-button\" href=\"/back-orderform/?id=1749432665-891410&amp;fav=1&amp;num=1\">\n              <span>カートに入れる</span>\n            </a>\n          </p>\n          \n          \n        </div>\n        \n      </div>\n    </div>\n    \n    \n    \n  </div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        \n        <table class=\"bd-table\">\n          \n          \n          <tbody><tr><th>著者・編者</th><td>Naganawa, Norihiro (ed.),</td></tr>\n          \n          \n          <tr><th>シリーズ</th><td>Imperial Encounters in Russian History</td></tr>\n          \n          \n          <tr><th>出版社</th><td>(Academic Studies Pr., US)</td></tr>\n          \n          \n          <tr><th>出版年月</th><td>2025.04</td></tr>\n          \n          \n          <tr><th>ページ数</th><td>290 pp.</td></tr>\n          \n          \n          <tr><th>言語</th><td>ENG</td></tr>\n          \n          \n          <tr><th>ニュース番号</th><td>＜100-6569 749-1554＞</td></tr>\n          \n        </tbody></table>\n        \n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    \n    \n    \n    <div class=\"bd-desc bd-desc-wide\">\n      <h3>解説</h3>\n      <div>Given Russia&#39;s invasion of Ukraine, why do emancipation messages that emanated from Russia count? Navigating multilingual sources, this book addresses the role of Russia&#39;s multiethnic society and borderlands in generating kaleidoscopic repercussions of its 1917 Revolution. It also sees the USSR&#39;s interactions with its neighboring countries as a crucible of the Soviet modality of communism. The book shows how the collapse of the Russian Empire further released a vast range of liberationist projects and dreams, far from confined to the goals of Bolshevism, in its borderlands and beyond, and how the Soviet Union became a highly ambiguous source of emancipatory inspiration in the long twentieth century overshadowing today&#39;s global politics.</div>\n    </div>\n    \n\n    \n    \n\n    \n    \n  </div></body></html>",
